WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.470 --> 00:00:05.210
- [Interviewer] Some of
these look a little more-

00:00:05.210 --> 00:00:06.130
- Yeah.

00:00:06.130 --> 00:00:08.690
- [Interviewer] Rough.
- It's hard out here, yeah.

00:00:08.690 --> 00:00:11.490
- [Interviewer] So, Ashley,
how long have you been here?

00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:13.990
- For five or six years.

00:00:13.990 --> 00:00:15.510
- [Interviewer] Five or six years.

00:00:15.510 --> 00:00:17.114
- Since I was 18.

00:00:17.114 --> 00:00:17.947
- [Interviewer] Since you were 18.

00:00:17.947 --> 00:00:18.839
How old are you now?

00:00:18.839 --> 00:00:21.113
- 25.
- [Interviewer] 25.

00:00:21.113 --> 00:00:23.713
- [Interviewer] Tell me
about your childhood.

00:00:23.713 --> 00:00:26.642
- [Ashley] Well, when I was
six, I went into foster care.

00:00:26.642 --> 00:00:27.475
- [Interviewer] Oh, you did?

00:00:27.475 --> 00:00:30.710
- Uh-huh. So I was in
and out of foster care

00:00:31.622 --> 00:00:35.130
'til I was like 13 and then once I was 13

00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:39.163
my grandma put me into foster
care first, permanently.

00:00:40.062 --> 00:00:41.150
- [Interviewer] And foster
care means what? You were...

00:00:41.150 --> 00:00:43.180
- Like she gave up. Because like...

00:00:43.180 --> 00:00:44.040
she gave up on the community.

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:45.480
- [Interviewer] Did you
have parents, at that point?

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:47.140
- My mom was a crack addict.

00:00:47.140 --> 00:00:50.840
My dad died of a heroin overdose
when I was six. So...yeah.

00:00:52.580 --> 00:00:54.750
And then I ran away from group homes

00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:58.137
and I was on the run from 13 to 18.

00:00:58.137 --> 00:00:58.990
- [Interviewer] Wow.

00:00:58.990 --> 00:01:01.225
- And then I was, yeah.

00:01:01.225 --> 00:01:02.327
- [Interviewer] And then
you ended up down here?

00:01:02.327 --> 00:01:03.704
- Yep.

00:01:03.704 --> 00:01:06.141
- [Interviewer] At some
point. And, you're living...?

00:01:06.141 --> 00:01:08.051
- I came down here looking for heroin,

00:01:08.051 --> 00:01:09.600
because I didn't know where to find it

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:11.880
when I came from Mexico. I was in Mexico

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:15.060
for a couple of years and
that's where I got strung out.

00:01:15.060 --> 00:01:16.623
And then I came back to LA,

00:01:17.470 --> 00:01:19.800
'cause me and my boyfriend broke up there

00:01:19.800 --> 00:01:22.890
and yeah, I didn't know
where to find any heroin.

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:24.920
So that's how I ended up on Skid Row.

00:01:24.920 --> 00:01:25.753
- [Interviewer] There's heroin here?

00:01:25.753 --> 00:01:26.586
- Yeah. Yeah.

00:01:29.620 --> 00:01:30.453
- [Interviewer] And heroin,

00:01:30.453 --> 00:01:31.950
you started doing at about age...

00:01:32.817 --> 00:01:34.330
- 18.
- [Interviewer] 18?

00:01:34.330 --> 00:01:36.210
- Yeah. So...no, 18 and...

00:01:36.210 --> 00:01:39.870
I came here when I was 19, so 18 and 19.

00:01:39.870 --> 00:01:41.340
It was a year. I was in Mexico,

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:44.680
strung out and then I
came straight from Mexico

00:01:44.680 --> 00:01:48.387
on the train to, what's
it called? Union Station?

00:01:48.387 --> 00:01:49.220
- [Interviewer] Union Station, right here.

00:01:49.220 --> 00:01:50.543
- [Ashley] Yeah, right here.

00:01:52.579 --> 00:01:53.879
- [Interviewer] And do you have a family,

00:01:53.879 --> 00:01:55.670
other than your siblings?

00:01:55.670 --> 00:02:00.670
- [Ashley] Yeah, I have two
sisters and two brothers.

00:02:00.680 --> 00:02:03.140
All younger, except my twin brother.

00:02:03.140 --> 00:02:04.397
He's one minute older.

00:02:04.397 --> 00:02:05.928
- [Interviewer] Did you talk to them?

00:02:05.928 --> 00:02:08.511
- [Ashley] Um...not really. No.

00:02:09.645 --> 00:02:11.830
- [Interviewer] And do
you have a boyfriend

00:02:11.830 --> 00:02:13.330
or anything like that down here?

00:02:13.330 --> 00:02:14.530
- [Ashley] I'm with a guy,

00:02:14.530 --> 00:02:17.810
I'm staying with a guy now in East LA.

00:02:17.810 --> 00:02:20.530
I met him down here. He's
not really my boyfriend,

00:02:20.530 --> 00:02:23.460
but I kind of have to like pretend he is,

00:02:23.460 --> 00:02:25.120
you know, to stay there.

00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:27.194
- [Interviewer] And what
are you doing for money?

00:02:27.194 --> 00:02:28.261
Like what's...the girls are doing...?

00:02:28.261 --> 00:02:29.161
- [Ashley] Prostitution.

00:02:29.161 --> 00:02:30.823
- [Interviewer] Yeah. How
long have you been doing that?

00:02:31.733 --> 00:02:32.566
Since about...

00:02:32.566 --> 00:02:35.033
- [Ashley] Since like, 19
since I came down here. Yeah.

00:02:37.387 --> 00:02:38.890
- [Interviewer] Do you
have crazy stories there?

00:02:38.890 --> 00:02:40.160
Because a lot of the girls have, like...

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:42.430
- [Ashley] Yeah. Well I got kidnapped

00:02:42.430 --> 00:02:44.253
for four days and raped.

00:02:45.110 --> 00:02:47.240
They took me over to
Hoover and Imperial Highway

00:02:47.240 --> 00:02:49.690
and held me there for like four days.

00:02:49.690 --> 00:02:51.600
And that's where I learned,

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:53.360
you know I learned a lot
from that experience,

00:02:53.360 --> 00:02:54.880
not to go with any Black guys,

00:02:54.880 --> 00:02:58.070
and to really trust my
intuition with the guys

00:02:58.070 --> 00:02:59.410
that I go with.

00:02:59.410 --> 00:03:04.300
So now, yeah, I don't
go with any Black guys.

00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:05.300
- [Interviewer] How'd you how'd you end up

00:03:05.300 --> 00:03:07.480
getting out of that situation?

00:03:07.480 --> 00:03:09.820
- [Ashley] Well, they were...the
guy and his girlfriend,

00:03:09.820 --> 00:03:10.760
They were high on meth.

00:03:10.760 --> 00:03:14.100
And so they fell asleep after four days

00:03:14.100 --> 00:03:16.910
and the girl left the
keys 'cause I was locked.

00:03:16.910 --> 00:03:20.060
It was all barred windows and barred...

00:03:20.060 --> 00:03:22.040
you know those black
doors, those screen doors

00:03:22.040 --> 00:03:23.177
that are metal?
- [Interviewer] Yeah.

00:03:23.177 --> 00:03:25.190
- And it had a lock from the inside

00:03:25.190 --> 00:03:28.170
and I snuck in the room and
I saw that the keys were

00:03:28.170 --> 00:03:32.160
inside this little plastic
Rubbermaid drawers.

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:32.993
I could see them.

00:03:32.993 --> 00:03:37.940
So I got a washcloth and I
picked up the keys quietly

00:03:37.940 --> 00:03:40.210
and there's like a thousand keys

00:03:40.210 --> 00:03:43.460
and I just tried them on
and I finally got out,

00:03:43.460 --> 00:03:47.220
and I just ran, with no
shoes and half-naked.

00:03:47.220 --> 00:03:48.520
Yeah. I looked so bad.

00:03:48.520 --> 00:03:50.070
It was really embarrassing.

00:03:50.070 --> 00:03:51.440
I was really sick.

00:03:51.440 --> 00:03:54.110
Really had to get something to get well.

00:03:54.110 --> 00:03:55.500
- [Interviewer] It's great
that you got out though.

00:03:55.500 --> 00:03:56.333
- Yeah, thank God.

00:03:56.333 --> 00:03:58.043
I don't know what they
were gonna do with me.

00:03:58.880 --> 00:04:01.470
They said they were going
to pimp me out, but...

00:04:01.470 --> 00:04:03.220
I don't think that they would
have been able to trust me.

00:04:03.220 --> 00:04:04.604
Maybe they would have
killed me or something.

00:04:04.604 --> 00:04:06.930
I don't know. It's really scary.

00:04:06.930 --> 00:04:08.753
So now, now I always have like,

00:04:10.220 --> 00:04:12.348
weapons with me and stuff.

00:04:12.348 --> 00:04:13.212
(interviewer laughs)

00:04:13.212 --> 00:04:14.453
- So I don't want that to ever happen.

00:04:14.453 --> 00:04:16.345
- [Interviewer] It's very dangerous.

00:04:16.345 --> 00:04:17.747
- Yeah, it is.

00:04:17.747 --> 00:04:18.890
- [Interviewer] Where would
you like to see yourself

00:04:18.890 --> 00:04:20.577
in five years? What would
you like to be doing?

00:04:20.577 --> 00:04:21.710
Do you have kids?

00:04:21.710 --> 00:04:22.700
- No.
- [Interviewer] No kids.

00:04:22.700 --> 00:04:24.000
- No, thank God.

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:26.710
I want kids, but not like this.

00:04:26.710 --> 00:04:28.720
Hopefully I'll be sober, you know,

00:04:28.720 --> 00:04:33.550
have my own place and have a job.

00:04:33.550 --> 00:04:35.480
Probably be just getting on my feet,

00:04:35.480 --> 00:04:38.770
but I like to be without a guy

00:04:38.770 --> 00:04:40.633
doing my own thing.

00:04:41.677 --> 00:04:42.510
- [Interviewer] Yeah.
Or a good guy, at least.

00:04:42.510 --> 00:04:43.590
- [Ashley] Yeah. A good guy.

00:04:43.590 --> 00:04:45.380
Not somebody I have to be with,

00:04:45.380 --> 00:04:47.690
Just like how I'm with this guy now.

00:04:47.690 --> 00:04:48.530
- [Interviewer] They're out there.

00:04:48.530 --> 00:04:49.640
- Yeah.

00:04:49.640 --> 00:04:50.473
- [Interviewer] Excellent.

00:04:50.473 --> 00:04:51.450
Well Ashley, thank you for talking to me.

00:04:51.450 --> 00:04:52.283
- Yeah! No problem.

00:04:52.283 --> 00:04:53.116
- [Interviewer] I appreciate it.

00:04:53.116 --> 00:04:53.949
- Thank you.

